WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.894 --> 00:00:21.917
Marius slowly climbed the steps to his apartment, his heart heavy with disappointment.

2
00:00:21.918 --> 00:00:27.829
"Monsieur Marius, you seem sad," said a voice behind him. "What's wrong?"

3
00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:36.059
At the top of the stairs, he turned around and found the older Jondrette girl. "Nothing's wrong," he said harshly. "Leave me alone."

4
00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:41.742
"No, you gave me something to eat; now let me help you," she pleaded.

5
00:00:41.743 --> 00:00:50.289
"I help my father all the time. Do you need me to deliver a message, or follow someone, or find out an address?"

6
00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:57.710
Marius realized that she might be useful after all. "You brought that old man and his daughter here. Do you know where they live?"

7
00:00:57.711 --> 00:01:07.305
"No, I met them at the church, but I can find out the address of the beautiful young lady if you wish."

8
00:01:07.306 --> 00:01:14.623
The bitterness with which she said "beautiful young lady" made Marius cringe, but he needed her assistance.

9
00:01:14.624 --> 00:01:16.882
"Yes, please do that for me."

10
00:01:16.883 --> 00:01:20.281
Marius entered his apartment and dropped into a chair.

11
00:01:20.282 --> 00:01:27.273
So much had happened since that morning. His angel had reappeared and then disappeared and now—

12
00:01:27.274 --> 00:01:31.186
"I tell you . . . I'm sure I recognized him!"

13
00:01:31.187 --> 00:01:36.606
Monsieur Jondrette's angry voice from the room next door cut suddenly through Marius' thoughts.

14
00:01:36.607 --> 00:01:41.424
Marius climbed upon the table once more and peered through his spy hole.

15
00:01:41.425 --> 00:01:47.257
Monsieur Jondrette had just come in and was taking off the coat that Monsieur Leblanc had given him.

16
00:01:47.258 --> 00:01:54.940
"Are you positive it's the same man?" asked Madame Jondrette. "Why didn't he recognize you?"

17
00:01:54.941 --> 00:01:57.583
Monsieur Jondrette stroked his beard.

18
00:01:57.584 --> 00:02:06.404
"Because I am in disguise, but even after all these years, I knew him immediately and the girl too.

19
00:02:06.405 --> 00:02:09.662
Don't you remember that girl who used to live with us?"

20
00:02:09.663 --> 00:02:16.496
"That girl!" Madame Jondrette's voice was a mixture of surprise, rage, and hatred.

21
00:02:16.497 --> 00:02:26.570
"Impossible! My daughters go barefoot and don't have a decent dress between them while her outfit must be worth at least two hundred francs!"

22
00:02:26.571 --> 00:02:30.243
"I'm telling you again that I recognized the two of them."

23
00:02:30.244 --> 00:02:33.309
Madame Jondrette shook her head in disbelief.

24
00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:43.294
"But Cosette used to be so ugly! You're saying she's that horrible, beautiful young lady who looked at my girls with such pity?

25
00:02:43.295 --> 00:02:47.191
Oh, I'd like to stomp her heart out!"

26
00:02:47.192 --> 00:02:51.997
"We'll do better than that, my dear. The old man will make us rich."

27
00:02:51.998 --> 00:02:54.532
Madame Jondrette looked puzzled.

28
00:02:54.533 --> 00:03:01.437
"It's all arranged," said her husband. "While I was out, I talked to some men and bought this."

29
00:03:01.438 --> 00:03:06.016
He showed her a chisel, and then laid the blade in the fire.

30
00:03:06.017 --> 00:03:10.778
"It may come in handy later if he won't cooperate."

31
00:03:10.779 --> 00:03:19.341
Marius could not believe what he was hearing. It appeared that Monsieur Leblanc—and perhaps Ursula too—was in grave danger.

32
00:03:19.342 --> 00:03:22.683
He slipped out of his apartment and went to the police station.

33
00:03:22.684 --> 00:03:28.008
"The chief of police isn't in," said an office boy when Marius arrived at the station.

34
00:03:28.009 --> 00:03:31.754
"But you can speak to an inspector if it's important."

35
00:03:31.755 --> 00:03:38.587
Marius nodded and the boy led him to an office, where a tall man was standing near the fire.

36
00:03:38.588 --> 00:03:41.650
"What do you want?" asked the inspector.

37
00:03:41.652 --> 00:03:45.000
"It's a very urgent matter," said Marius.

38
00:03:45.001 --> 00:03:47.267
"Then you'd better speak quickly."

39
00:03:47.268 --> 00:03:52.976
Marius told the inspector how he'd overheard the plot to ambush Monsieur Leblanc.

40
00:03:52.977 --> 00:03:59.159
He didn't know Leblanc's real name or address, but he was sure that the old man was in danger.

41
00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:04.730
This was all going to take place at six o'clock in the old Gorbeau house.

42
00:04:04.731 --> 00:04:09.223
The inspector raised his eyebrows. "The old Gorbeau house?"

43
00:04:09.224 --> 00:04:10.905
"Are you familiar with it?"

44
00:04:10.906 --> 00:04:15.801
"Indeed I am." The inspector reached into a drawer and pulled out a pistol.

45
00:04:15.802 --> 00:04:19.801
"Take this and go back to spying from your room.

46
00:04:19.802 --> 00:04:27.627
My men and I will be hiding in the neighborhood. When the situation is at its most dangerous, fire the pistol and we'll rush in."

47
00:04:27.628 --> 00:04:31.690
Marius took the gun and hid it in his waistcoat.

48
00:04:31.691 --> 00:04:41.524
"By the way," said the policeman, "if you need me before then, send a message to me here. My name is Inspector Javert."

49
00:04:41.525 --> 00:04:45.762
Marius went home and tiptoed into his apartment.

50
00:04:45.763 --> 00:04:49.437
There was only half an hour before Leblanc was due to return.

51
00:04:49.438 --> 00:04:55.524
As Marius climbed on top of his table, he could hear Monsieur Jondrette quizzing his daughters.

52
00:04:55.525 --> 00:04:59.937
"You saw the housekeeper go out, but what about the fellow next door?"

53
00:04:59.938 --> 00:05:03.461
"I heard him leave a while ago," said the older daughter.

54
00:05:03.462 --> 00:05:09.334
"He always goes out for his supper around this time and stays away for several hours."

55
00:05:09.335 --> 00:05:12.675
"You'd better check just to be sure."

56
00:05:12.676 --> 00:05:20.826
Marius dropped to his hands and knees and silently crawled under his bed. He'd just hidden himself when he saw his door open.

57
00:05:20.827 --> 00:05:25.686
"He's gone out, Papa," said the older girl. "His key is in the door."

58
00:05:25.687 --> 00:05:28.667
"Go in anyway," called her father.

59
00:05:28.668 --> 00:05:35.477
The girl entered the room with a candle and walked straight toward the bed. But she didn't look under it.

60
00:05:35.478 --> 00:05:41.144
Instead she headed for the mirror, where she gazed at herself and hummed a song.

61
00:05:41.145 --> 00:05:47.818
Meanwhile Marius was trembling under the bed. He couldn't believe that she didn't hear him breathing.

62
00:05:47.819 --> 00:05:52.556
"What are you doing over there?" called Monsieur Jondrette from next door.

63
00:05:52.557 --> 00:05:59.469
"I'm checking under all the furniture," said the daughter as she continued to arrange her hair in the mirror.

64
00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:03.118
"Come back here! It's time for you to go out."

65
00:06:03.119 --> 00:06:06.953
The girl left and Marius crawled from under the bed.

66
00:06:06.954 --> 00:06:13.700
He dusted himself off and climbed the table just in time to hear Jondrette giving instructions to his daughters.

67
00:06:13.701 --> 00:06:20.683
They were to stand guard at each end of the street and come back immediately at the first sign of anything strange.

68
00:06:20.684 --> 00:06:25.088
The girls left and Jondrette began to pace the room.

69
00:06:25.089 --> 00:06:30.024
"Do you know what we need?" he said to his wife. "Two more chairs."

70
00:06:30.025 --> 00:06:33.858
"No problem. I'll get them from the neighbor's."

71
00:06:33.859 --> 00:06:42.175
Before Marius could hide under the bed, Madame Jondrette had entered his apartment. Fortunately she had not brought a candle.

72
00:06:42.176 --> 00:06:49.508
Marius flattened himself against the wall while she went directly to his chairs, picked them up, and left the room.

73
00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:54.508
Marius did not dare to breathe until she was safely on the other side of the wall.

74
00:06:54.509 --> 00:06:59.322
"Good!" said Monsieur Jondrette as he arranged the chairs facing each other.

75
00:06:59.322 --> 00:07:04.238
"Now take this lantern downstairs and wait for our guest."

76
00:07:04.239 --> 00:07:07.905
Marius peered around the Jondrettes' darkened room.

77
00:07:07.906 --> 00:07:17.992
He noticed a pile of rope and some metal objects on the floor, but he didn't recognize them for what they were: burglar's tools.

78
00:07:17.993 --> 00:07:24.135
Jondrette pulled a long carving knife from a drawer in the table and ran his finger along the edge.

79
00:07:24.136 --> 00:07:29.222
Then he hid it away again and sat down in one of Marius' chairs.

80
00:07:29.223 --> 00:07:37.135
For his part, Marius took the pistol from his pocket and cocked it. The gun made a distinct click.

81
00:07:37.136 --> 00:07:41.381
Jondrette started and half rose from his chair. "Who's there?"

82
00:07:41.382 --> 00:07:50.932
Marius didn't dare to move. Jondrette listened for a moment and then began to laugh.

83
00:07:50.933 --> 00:07:55.131
"What a fool I am! It's just the wall creaking."

84
00:07:55.132 --> 00:07:58.369
Marius kept his pistol in his hand.

85
00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:05.227
A church clock struck six o'clock, and Marius heard the sound of a carriage arriving outside.
